WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.240
(casting)

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:30.551
Imagine going from back-to-back relegation
tournaments, and fighting for survival in

00:00:30.551 --> 00:00:34.050
your own league, to winning the entire thing.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.790
Well you don’t have to imagine.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:43.570
I’m Colin McNeil, and today we’re talking
about Team Liquid’s 2018 NA LCS Spring Split

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:44.570
run.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:49.960
Now, if you’re a TL fan already, I don’t need to tell
you, the boys in blue have not always had

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:50.960
it easy.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.640
That’s why our story starts last year, in
two very unsuccessful splits for Team Liquid.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:16.800
(casting)

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.520
But things were looking up in 2018.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.960
First, Team Liquid secured that coveted franchise
spot in the new league.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.000
And 
the hype surrounding Doublelift, Pobelter,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.920
Impact, Xmithie, and Olleh, meant the 
team

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.040
was coming in hot to 
the spring split.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.040
And, at least at first, they did not disappoint.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:04:07.120
(casting)

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.720
Now, it was around week 4 however, if you remember, that the shine came off Team Liquid.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:19.520
They faced down their first 0-2 week in the split,
and the following weeks had them find consistently

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.019
inconsistent results.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:07:52.080
(casting)

00:07:52.080 --> 00:08:00.080
Now much to the relief of Team Liquid fans everywhere, it was in week 9 against 
Cloud9 they locked in that playoff spot.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:09:25.760
(casting)

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:31.360
Okay, so TL squeaks into the playoffs, but they get in.

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:38.080
Facing down the likes of TSM, Cloud9, 100 Thieves and Echo Fox though, things were not going to be easy.

00:09:38.080 --> 00:12:03.840
(casting)

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:10.080
Personal tragedy struck Doublelift before the grand finals, and there were some questions as to whether

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.320
or not he'd be able to play in them or not.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:14.240
Well he did play.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.560
And he was lights out.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:21.360
In fact, the entirety of Team Liquid hit the rift like players possessed.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:26.400
They 3-0'd 100 Thieves, sweeping them, in the grand final.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:15:40.560
(casting)

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.480
And that's how they did it.

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:44.640
That's how Team Liquid broke their curse.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.880
They weren't fourth anymore.

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:53.600
They raised their banner, lifted the trophy and became the fourth ever team to win  NA LCS.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.760
The fourth.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.600
Sh-t.

